===Noun===
'''virii''' {{p}}

# {{proscribed}} {{irregular plural of|[[virus]]}}
# {{computing|nonstandard}} A superset of computer software composed of computer [[virus|viruses]], [[trojan|trojans]], and [[worms]].

====Usage notes====
*The plural {{term|virii}}, though common among [[geek]]s and [[nerd]]s, is incorrect and based on several misunderstandings of Latin: 1. [[masculine|Masculine]] Latin words in -us form the plural in -i, not in -ii. "Virii" could be the plural of a ([[hypothetical]], non-existing) masculine word "virius". 2. {{term|virus|lang=la}} was a [[neutral]] word in Latin, neutral words ending in -us form the plural in -us (e.g. {{term|casus|lang=la}} - {{term|casus|lang=la}}). 3. The Latin word {{term|virus|lang=la}} did not have a plural at all, it was an [[uncountable]] noun meaning "poison". Using the English pluralisation rules to yield '''[[viruses]]''' is therefore the only correct way.

*'''[[viri|Viri]]''' is also not the (Latin) plural of virus, but the plural of {{term|vir|lang=la}}, which means ''man''.

